{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And the one who gathers shall wash.</b> According to the plain sense, the one who gathers requires washing of garments, but the one who deposits the ashes outside the camp does not require washing of garments, because the work of the ashes was completed before his action. And because it is impossible to gather without some of it flying onto the garment of the gatherer, and the ashes are sacred. And lest he carry it to an unclean place, he requires washing of garments, as it is written regarding the sin-offering: ״and he who sprinkles from the blood upon the garment shall wash it,״ etc. — and likewise regarding the bull and the goat that are burned, and likewise the one who throws and burns, for this reason; and likewise the one who touches and the one who carries and the one who sprinkles require washing — lest some of the waters of sprinkling have gone upon him or upon his garments." "<b>And the one who gathers shall wash.</b> Why is this stated? If the one who throws the hyssop defiles garments, the one who gathers the ashes — is it not all the more so? But if you say so, you would be punishing by inference; therefore ״and the one who gathers shall wash״ is stated, to teach you that one does not punish by inference. Another interpretation: come and learn concerning the one who gathers, that he defiles by shifting. And even though with other sacred offerings, once they have become ash there is no sanctity in them — that is because there is no benefit in the ashes; but here, the entire essence is in the ashes, and it defiles forever, so that people keep away from it." "<b>And the one who gathers shall wash his garments.</b> All the more so his flesh — and the verse proves it, as it is written: <b>and he is unclean until evening.</b> This implies that he had already bathed, for had he not bathed, his uncleanness would remain upon him forever. And a parallel to this we find: ״and the clean one shall sprinkle upon the unclean, and he shall wash his garments and bathe his flesh and be clean at evening.״"], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:42.057862791Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}